// THE WORKERS' TIMERS (row 483; the spec is "aio and http"'s worker-timers
// spec, 18 Nov 2026). A scheduler service: a timer awaited on a worker is a
// CELL in that worker's own store, armed in that worker's own timewheel, and
// fired by that worker between its turns, its answer going to its own queue.
// Nothing crosses to aio's I/O thread and nothing is locked across workers on
// the common path. aio's sleeps are its first user (timerAwaitable); the
// re-armable Timer holds one of the same cells for its life (THE HELD TIMER,
// below).
//
// A STORE, one per worker index, made by the worker at its first timer and
// never freed (a group that outlives the runtime may still signal a cell's
// Wakeup, which must then find the cell's generation moved, not freed memory;
// aio's record pool lives the same way). It holds:
//   - the cells, in chunks of cellsPerChunk, never unmapped, and the owner's
//     free list of them (no lock: only the owner takes and frees);
//   - the wheel (timewheel.Wheel), an entry per armed cell, its token the
//     cell's address (the low three bits are clear: a later kind bit's room);
//     the owner's, under THE WHEEL WORD (below);
//   - the RETIRE STACK, an atomic head: a cell resolved or let go on another
//     thread is pushed there (one CAS) and the owner frees it at its next step;
//   - 'armed', the cells armed now, which any thread lowers by its winning CAS;
//   - 'sweep', set by the worker's own Wakeup when an ANCESTOR of a cell's group
//     is cancelled (cancelgroups' watchWorkerAbove): the owner then looks at
//     every armed cell's group;
//   - 'due', the instant the owner must wake at, published while it parks, for
//     THE POLLER (poller.cone), which keeps time for parked workers and fires
//     their due cells as their deputy (THE PARK, below); nonzero says parked.
// The step (timersStep) is the store's one entry for the owner: the retired
// cells freed, a sweep if asked, and the due cells fired; or, once the stop has
// begun, every armed cell dropped.
//
// A CELL'S WORD is its generation (above the low 8 bits) and its state:
//   Free -> Ready (made by an Awaitable, not yet awaited: it holds the asking)
//   Ready -> Armed (awaited on its owner: it holds the await's Reply, is in the
//            wheel and registered in its group)
//   Armed -> Taken (by ONE compare-and-swap, whoever makes it: the owner's fire,
//            the owner's sweep, the stop's drop, or a cancel on any thread)
//   Ready -> Dead (the Awaitable dropped off its owner, or awaited on another
//            worker, which takes a fresh cell of its own)
//   and back to Free, generation moved, by the owner alone.
// EXACTLY ONCE: the Reply is taken only by the CAS out of Armed, so it is
// answered or let go once; the loser of the CAS does nothing to it. The winner
// has the cell to itself until it frees it (the owner) or pushes it on the
// retire stack (any other thread), which the owner drains. A cell's Wakeup in
// its group's registry names it by address and the word it was armed with, so
// one that outlives the arming finds the word moved and does nothing ('isGone'
// is true, and watchHere's sweep drops it).
//
// THE WHEEL WORD (row 485) is a one-word lock ('lock') round every operation on
// the wheel and on 'next': the owner takes it uncontended (one compare-and-swap
// a side, about 10-20 ns), and the monitor takes it only by try-lock, for THE
// DEPUTY. The owner waits if it finds it held, which is only while the deputy
// has the wheel's overdue entries out: a bounded pass with no answer inside it.
//
// THE DEPUTY. A worker in a long turn fires nothing, so its cells are late by
// the rest of the turn, which today's I/O-thread timers never are. The monitor
// already finds a worker that has held one turn for a whole tick (THE MONITOR),
// and then looks at its store (timersDeputy): if the worker is not parked (its
// 'due' is 0: a parked worker's cells are the poller's, below) and its
// 'next' has passed, the monitor try-locks the wheel and takes the due entries
// out; each cell is taken by the same CAS out of Armed as every fire, so a
// cancel racing the deputy answers once, whichever wins. With the lock let go,
// the monitor answers the cells it won from its own thread (the answer goes to
// the inject queue, as a cancel's does from a plain thread, and any worker
// runs it) and retires them to the owner, which frees them at its next step:
// only the owner touches the free list. A deputy's fires are counted apart
// ('deputyFires') and added to 'fires' by timerStats. A stuck worker's cell is
// late by at most the wheel's tick and the monitor's own (spec section 6).
//
// THE ANSWERS, as aio's sleeps have always given them: due at its time, Done;
// a deadline (the IoLimits' or its group's, the tighter) before that, TimedOut
// at the deadline; the group's cancel, Cancelled at once (TimedOut if the cause
// is TimedOut, the group's deadline); one already cancelled, or due already,
// answered in the start itself, in the same batch. The answer is made by the
// caller's function (aio's), told timerDone, timerCancelled or timerTimedOut.
//
// WHO ANSWERS: the fire and the sweep, the owner, onto its own queue; a cancel,
// the cancelling thread (choice 5), as orCancelled's does. The actor cannot
// end with a live cell: the Reply holds a count of it.
//
// THE PARK (row 493, which replaced row 483's interim, the monitor keeping time
// for parked workers). A worker with armed cells publishes its earliest in
// 'due' before it parks. The worker that holds THE POLLER ROLE (poller.cone)
// waits in the runtime's worker port, bounded by its own cells and every
// parked worker's (its one high-resolution timer: a beat of about 0.5 ms on
// Windows, the timerfd's nanoseconds on Linux), and fires the parked workers'
// due cells as their DEPUTY under the wheel word, answering onto its own queue:
// one wake for a parked worker's cell, and it is late by at most a wheel tick
// and the timer's beat. While nobody holds the role the monitor wakes the
// parked owner of the earliest cell by name (THE GAP). With no port (the
// system gave none) a parked worker bounds its own futex wait by its cell, as
// row 483 had it. A runtime of one worker takes cells too: its one worker
// always holds the role. A runtime of several workers with no monitor
// (Options.monitorMicros 0) takes none: timerAwaitable says None, and aio keeps
// its I/O thread's timer.
//
// THE STOP. stopWorkers sets timersStopped first: from then no cell fires, no
// cancel answers one, and a timer started is let go unanswered at once, as aio
// abandons what is still awaited at its end. Each worker with armed cells is
// woken and drops them at its step, the Replies let go unanswered (the awaiting
// behaviour abandoned, as at the end); the stop waits until every store's
// 'armed' is 0, the workers still running, before it goes on. The runtime is
// never started again, so the stores are not reused. A sweep asked for and not yet made is let go as well (the
// step clears it, and idle does not count it as work once the timers have stopped): a worker must reach its
// 'stopping' check, which a standing ask would otherwise keep it from for ever (row 531).

// A cell's states, the low 8 bits of its word
// (Free is 0: cellFree, the function, leaves a free cell's state 0)
const cellReady = 1u64;
const cellArmed = 2u64;
const cellTaken = 3u64;
const cellDead = 4u64;
const cellHeld = 5u64;         // held by a Timer for its life (THE HELD TIMER): its own word is 'hword'
const cellStateMask = 0xFFu64;
const cellGenStep = 0x100u64;

// A cell's flags
const cellRelative = 1u32;     // 'at' is nanoseconds counted from the await, not an instant
const cellLapses = 2u32;       // its due is a deadline before its time: it answers TimedOut

const cellsPerChunk = 64usize;

// What a timer's answer function is told (timerAwaitable)
const timerDone = 0u32;
const timerCancelled = 1u32;
const timerTimedOut = 2u32;

// No instant: a store with nothing armed
const noDue = 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFi64;

struct TimerCell {
  word: Atomic[u64];          // generation and state (above)
  free: *TimerCell;           // the owner's free list
  retired: *TimerCell;        // the retire stack
  store: *TimerStore;         // the owner's store
  entry: TimerId;             // its wheel entry while armed (the owner's)
  at: i64;                    // the instant asked for, in nanoseconds; with cellRelative, the wait from the await
  limit: i64;                 // the IoLimits' deadline, in nanoseconds
  flags: u32;
  reply: Reply;               // the await's, while Armed
  group: Option[CancelGroup]; // the IoLimits' group, from Ready until freed
  answer: &fn(rp: &mut Reply, outcome: u32);
  hword: Atomic[u64];         // a held cell's word (THE HELD TIMER)
  want: Atomic[i64];          // a held cell's deadline, noDue for none: written by its holder only
  hentry: Atomic[u64];        // a held cell's live wheel entry (a TimerId's word), written by whoever holds hBusy
}

struct TimerChunk {
  next: *TimerChunk;
  cells: *TimerCell;
}

struct TimerStore {
  before: Array[u8, 64];
  retire: Atomic[usize];      // the retire stack's head: pushed by any thread, taken whole by the owner
  sweep: Atomic[u32];         // an ancestor's cancel reached this worker
  index: u32;
  armed: Atomic[u64];         // cells Armed now
  due: Atomic[i64];           // the owner's earliest instant, published while it parks; 0 none
  gap: Array[u8, 32];
  wheel: Wheel;               // the owner's
  free: *TimerCell;           // the owner's
  chunks: *TimerChunk;        // every chunk, newest first (the sweep's and the drop's walk)
  lock: Atomic[u32];          // THE WHEEL WORD: 1 while the wheel and 'next' are held
  next: Atomic[i64];          // when the owner must next call its wheel's expired: noDue when it is empty (set under the lock; the monitor reads it)
  expiries: List[Expiry];     // the owner's scratch
  arms: Atomic[u64];          // counts, the owner's (Relaxed), for timerStats
  fires: Atomic[u64];
  deputyFires: Atomic[u64];   // fired by the monitor as the owner's deputy (its Relaxed add)
  cancels: Atomic[u64];       // answered Cancelled or TimedOut by a cancel or a sweep, any thread
  dropped: Atomic[u64];       // let go unanswered at the stop
  waiters: Atomic[u64];       // held cells of this store's with a next() parked (THE HELD TIMER), any thread
  held: Atomic[u64];          // this store's cells held by a Timer now, any thread
  heldIn: Atomic[u64];        // held cells' entries put in this wheel, and taken out (expired or cancelled): the owner's
  heldOut: Atomic[u64];
  movesInPlace: Atomic[u64];  // earlier moves made in this wheel by cancel and insert, the owner's
  movesAcross: Atomic[u64];   // earlier moves that left a dead entry in another worker's wheel (or asked its filer)
  refiles: Atomic[u64];       // held entries come up early (a later move) and filed again here
  deadEntries: Atomic[u64];   // held entries come up dead, discarded here
}

// The stores, by worker index: an array of addresses made at startWorkers, never freed
let timerTable: Atomic[usize];
let timerTableLen: Atomic[u32];
// 1 from the stop's first step (THE STOP, above)
let timersStopped: Atomic[u32];
// This worker's store, or 0
var @threadlocal myTimers: usize = 0usize;

fn noAnswer(rp: &mut Reply, outcome: u32) {}

// The table for n workers, at startWorkers
fn timerTableMake(n: u32) {
  let t = libc.calloc(usize.from(n), mem.sizeof[usize]()) as usize;
  if t == 0usize {
    die("actors: out of memory for the runtime");
  }
  timerTableLen.store(0u32);
  timerTable.store(t);
  timerTableLen.store(n);
}

// Worker i's store, or 0 if it has made none (any thread)
fn timerStoreOf(i: u32) *TimerStore {
  if i >= timerTableLen.load() {
    return null;
  }
  let t = timerTable.load();
  mem.atomicLoad[usize]((t + usize.from(i) * mem.sizeof[usize]()) as *usize, MemOrder.Acquire) as *TimerStore
}

// This worker's store, made at its first timer; 0 off the workers
fn timersHere() *TimerStore {
  if myTimers != 0usize {
    return myTimers as *TimerStore;
  }
  let w = me as *Worker;
  if w as usize == 0usize || (*w).index >= timerTableLen.load() {
    return null;
  }
  let ts = libc.calloc(1usize, mem.sizeof[TimerStore]()) as *TimerStore;
  if ts as usize == 0usize {
    die("actors: out of memory for a worker's timers");
  }
  (*ts).retire = Atomic[usize].of(0usize);
  (*ts).sweep = Atomic[u32].of(0u32);
  (*ts).index = (*w).index;
  (*ts).armed = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).due = Atomic[i64].of(0i64);
  mem.writeRaw[Wheel](&(*ts).wheel as *Wheel, Wheel.make(time.Instant.now()));
  (*ts).free = null;
  (*ts).chunks = null;
  (*ts).lock = Atomic[u32].of(0u32);
  (*ts).next = Atomic[i64].of(noDue);
  mem.writeRaw[List[Expiry]](&(*ts).expiries as *List[Expiry], List[Expiry]());
  (*ts).arms = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).fires = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).deputyFires = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).cancels = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).dropped = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).waiters = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).held = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).heldIn = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).heldOut = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).movesInPlace = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).movesAcross = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).refiles = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  (*ts).deadEntries = Atomic[u64].of(0u64);
  let t = timerTable.load();
  mem.atomicStore[usize]((t + usize.from((*w).index) * mem.sizeof[usize]()) as *usize, ts as usize, MemOrder.Release);
  myTimers = ts as usize;
  ts
}

// A Ready cell from the owner's free list (a new chunk when it is empty)
fn cellTake(ts: *TimerStore) *TimerCell {
  if (*ts).free as usize == 0usize {
    let size = mem.sizeof[TimerCell]();
    let block = libc.malloc(cellsPerChunk * size) as *TimerCell;
    let ch = libc.malloc(mem.sizeof[TimerChunk]()) as *TimerChunk;
    if block as usize == 0usize || ch as usize == 0usize {
      die("actors: out of memory for a worker's timers");
    }
    var i = cellsPerChunk;
    while i > 0usize {
      i = i - 1usize;
      let c = block + i;
      mem.writeRaw[TimerCell](c, TimerCell(Atomic[u64].of(cellGenStep), (*ts).free, null, ts,
        TimerId.none(), 0i64, 0i64, 0u32, Reply(), None, &noAnswer,
        Atomic[u64].of(0u64), Atomic[i64].of(noDue), Atomic[u64].of(0u64)));
      (*ts).free = c;
    }
    (*ch).next = (*ts).chunks;
    (*ch).cells = block;
    (*ts).chunks = ch;
  }
  let c = (*ts).free;
  (*ts).free = (*c).free;
  (*c).free = null;
  (*c).word.store(((*c).word.load() & ~cellStateMask) | cellReady);
  c
}

// THE WHEEL WORD: the owner waits for it (the deputy holds it for a bounded
// pass and answers nothing inside); the monitor only tries
fn wheelLock(ts: *TimerStore) {
  var spins = 0u32;
  while true {
    let seen, ok = (*ts).lock.compareSwap(0u32, 1u32);
    if ok {
      return;
    }
    spins = spins + 1u32;
    if spins < 200u32 {
      yieldProcessor();
    } else {
      thread.sleep(time.Duration.fromMicros(20i64));
    }
  }
}

fn wheelTry(ts: *TimerStore) bool {
  let seen, ok = (*ts).lock.compareSwap(0u32, 1u32);
  ok
}

fn wheelUnlock(ts: *TimerStore) {
  (*ts).lock.store(0u32);
}

// When the owner must next call its wheel's expired
fn nextOf(ts: *TimerStore) i64 {
  (*ts).next.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed)
}

// 'next' from the wheel's own earliest, noDue when it is empty (the lock held)
fn nextSet(ts: *TimerStore) {
  let wh = &(*ts).wheel;
  match wh.nextExpiry() {
    case let Some(t) {(*ts).next.storeOrdered(t.nanos(), MemOrder.Relaxed);}
    else {(*ts).next.storeOrdered(noDue, MemOrder.Relaxed);}
  }
}

// The cell back on the owner's free list, its group let go and its generation
// moved (the owner)
fn cellFree(ts: *TimerStore, c: *TimerCell) {
  wheelLock(ts);
  if !(*c).entry.isNone() {
    let wh = &mut (*ts).wheel;
    wh.cancel((*c).entry);
    (*c).entry = TimerId.none();
  }
  wheelUnlock(ts);
  cellRecycle(ts, c);
}

// The same for a cell in no wheel (its entry none)
fn cellRecycle(ts: *TimerStore, c: *TimerCell) {
  let g = mem.readRaw[Option[CancelGroup]](&(*c).group as *Option[CancelGroup]);
  mem.writeRaw[Option[CancelGroup]](&(*c).group as *Option[CancelGroup], None[CancelGroup]);
  let w = (*c).word.load();
  (*c).word.store((w & ~cellStateMask) + cellGenStep);
  (*c).free = (*ts).free;
  (*ts).free = c;
}

// The await's Reply out of the cell, which keeps a blank (the CAS's winner)
fn cellReply(c: *TimerCell) Reply {
  let r = mem.readRaw[Reply](&(*c).reply as *Reply);
  mem.writeRaw[Reply](&(*c).reply as *Reply, Reply());
  r
}

// A cell resolved or let go off its owner: on the retire stack, for the owner
// to free. The caller has the cell to itself and does not touch it after
fn cellRetire(c: *TimerCell) {
  let ts = (*c).store;
  while true {
    let h = (*ts).retire.load();
    (*c).retired = h as *TimerCell;
    let seen, ok = (*ts).retire.compareSwap(h, c as usize);
    if ok {
      return;
    }
  }
}

// What a cancel answers: TimedOut when the cause is the group's deadline, else Cancelled
fn cancelOutcome(g: &Option[CancelGroup]) u32 {
  match *g {
    case let Some(x) {
      match x.cause() {
        case let Some(c) {
          match c {
            case Cause.TimedOut {return timerTimedOut;}
            else {}
          }
        }
        else {}
      }
    }
    else {}
  }
  timerCancelled
}

// Whether the cell's group is cancelled (an ancestor's included)
fn cellCancelled(c: *TimerCell) bool {
  match (*c).group {
    case let Some(g) {g.isCancelled()}
    else {false}
  }
}

// A cell's Wakeup in its own group (cancelgroups' watchHere): the cancel, on
// whatever thread it runs and under the group's lock, takes the cell's Reply
// by the CAS out of Armed and answers it there (choice 5), then retires the
// cell to its owner. Sendable on trust: it names the cell, which is never
// freed, and the word it was armed with
struct CellWake is Sendable {
  cell: *TimerCell;
  word: u64;

  pub fn signal(self: &) bool {
    if timersStopped.load() != 0u32 {
      return false;
    }
    let c = cell;
    let seen, ok = (*c).word.compareSwap(word, (word & ~cellStateMask) | cellTaken);
    if !ok {
      return false;
    }
    let ts = (*c).store;
    (*ts).armed.sub(1u64);
    (*ts).cancels.addOrdered(1u64, MemOrder.Relaxed);
    let o = cancelOutcome(&(*c).group);
    var r = cellReply(c);
    let f = (*c).answer;
    f(&mut r, o);
    cellRetire(c);
    true
  }

  pub fn isGone(self: &) bool {(*cell).word.load() != word}
}

// A worker's Wakeup in the ancestors of its cells' groups (cancelgroups'
// watchWorkerAbove): one per worker index for the life of the process, as
// watchWorker asks. The cancel asks the worker to sweep, and wakes it if it is
// parked; never gone
struct WorkerWake is Sendable {
  index: u32;

  pub fn signal(self: &) bool {
    if timersStopped.load() != 0u32 {
      return false;
    }
    let ts = timerStoreOf(index);
    if ts as usize == 0usize {
      return false;
    }
    (*ts).sweep.store(1u32);
    wakeWorkerAt(index);
    true
  }

  pub fn isGone(self: &) bool {false}
}

// Wake worker i if it is parked: its bit claimed, its word PARKED to NOTIFIED,
// as wakeOne does for whichever worker. Any thread; a plain one passes THE
// STOP'S GATE, as opSpent's wake does. A worker not parked sees what the caller
// stored before this, SeqCst, at its look after it publishes its park (idle)
fn wakeWorkerAt(i: u32) {
  let plain = me == 0usize && stopperHere == 0usize;
  if plain && !gateEnter() {
    return;
  }
  let s = running.load() as *Sched;
  if s as usize != 0usize && i < (*s).nworkers {
    wakeNamed(s, workerAt(s, i));
  }
  if plain {
    gateLeave();
  }
}

fn wakeNamed(s: *Sched, w: *Worker) {
  let wp = parkedWord(s, (*w).index / 64u32);
  let bit = parkedBit(w);
  if (mem.atomicAnd[u64](wp, ~bit, MemOrder.SeqCst) & bit) != 0u64 {
    let seen, marked = (*w).park.compareSwap(parkParked, parkNotified);
    if marked {
      // Its futex word, or a break if it waits in the port (poller.cone)
      wakeMarked(w);
    }
  }
}

// The I/O layer's entry onto the timer service, called by aio, not by programs
// (public because aio calls it from its own package, as answerNowIn and
// workerHooks are): a timer awaited on the worker
// that awaits it, as a CELL of that worker's (THE WORKERS' TIMERS, timers.cone).
// 'when' is an instant in nanoseconds, or, if 'relative', nanoseconds counted
// from the await; 'group' and 'limit' are the IoLimits' (copied); 'answer' is
// called once with the await's Reply and timerDone (0), timerCancelled (1) or
// timerTimedOut (2), on the thread that decides it, and answers R through
// answerNowIn. None, the caller to keep its own timer, off the workers, in a
// runtime of several workers with no monitor (Options.monitorMicros 0), and
// once the stop has begun. A runtime of one worker has cells (row 493 (b)): its
// one worker always holds the poller's role when it parks, and keeps its own
// time in the port
pub fn timerAwaitable[R](when: i64, relative: bool, group: &Option[CancelGroup], limit: time.Instant,
    answer: &fn(rp: &mut Reply, outcome: u32)) Option[Awaitable[R]] {
  let w = me as *Worker;
  if w as usize == 0usize || timersStopped.load() != 0u32 {
    return None;
  }
  let s = (*w).sched;
  if (*s).monitorMicros == 0u32 && (*s).nworkers != 1u32 {
    return None;
  }
  let ts = timersHere();
  if ts as usize == 0usize {
    return None;
  }
  let c = cellTake(ts);
  (*c).at = when;
  (*c).limit = limit.nanos();
  (*c).flags = if relative {cellRelative} else {0u32};
  mem.writeRaw[Option[CancelGroup]](&(*c).group as *Option[CancelGroup], *group);
  (*c).answer = answer;
  Some[Awaitable[R]](Awaitable[R].of(c as *u8, &timerStart, &timerDrop))
}

// An Awaitable's cell let go unawaited: freed by its owner, or retired to it
fn timerDrop(ctx: *u8) {
  let c = ctx as *TimerCell;
  cellLetGo(c);
}

// A Ready cell let go by its one holder: on the owner, freed; elsewhere its
// group let go here and the cell retired Dead
fn cellLetGo(c: *TimerCell) {
  let ts = (*c).store;
  if myTimers == ts as usize {
    cellFree(ts, c);
    return;
  }
  let g = mem.readRaw[Option[CancelGroup]](&(*c).group as *Option[CancelGroup]);
  mem.writeRaw[Option[CancelGroup]](&(*c).group as *Option[CancelGroup], None[CancelGroup]);
  (*c).word.store(((*c).word.load() & ~cellStateMask) | cellDead);
  cellRetire(c);
}

// The await: the cell armed on this worker (a fresh one of its own if the
// Awaitable was made on another), or answered at once
fn timerStart(ctx: *u8, rp: Reply) {
  var c = ctx as *TimerCell;
  var r = rp;
  let ts = timersHere();
  if ts as usize == 0usize || timersStopped.load() != 0u32 {
    // Off the workers (no await runs there), or the stop has begun: let go
    // unanswered, as aio abandons an operation after its end
    cellLetGo(c);
    return;
  }
  if (*c).store as usize != ts as usize {
    // Made on another worker: a cell of this one's, the old one retired
    let n = cellTake(ts);
    (*n).at = (*c).at;
    (*n).limit = (*c).limit;
    (*n).flags = (*c).flags;
    (*n).answer = (*c).answer;
    mem.writeRaw[Option[CancelGroup]](&(*n).group as *Option[CancelGroup],
      mem.readRaw[Option[CancelGroup]](&(*c).group as *Option[CancelGroup]));
    mem.writeRaw[Option[CancelGroup]](&(*c).group as *Option[CancelGroup], None[CancelGroup]);
    (*c).word.store(((*c).word.load() & ~cellStateMask) | cellDead);
    cellRetire(c);
    c = n;
  }
  let now = time.Instant.now().nanos();
  var at = (*c).at;
  if ((*c).flags & cellRelative) != 0u32 {
    at = if at > noDue - now {noDue} else {now + at};
  }
  var dl = (*c).limit;
  match (*c).group {
    case let Some(g) {
      if g.deadline().nanos() < dl {dl = g.deadline().nanos();}
    }
    else {}
  }
  var due = at;
  var lapses = false;
  if dl < at {
    due = dl;
    lapses = true;
  }
  let f = (*c).answer;
  if cellCancelled(c) {
    let o = cancelOutcome(&(*c).group);
    cellFree(ts, c);
    f(&mut r, o);
    return;
  }
  if due <= now {
    cellFree(ts, c);
    f(&mut r, if lapses {timerTimedOut} else {timerDone});
    return;
  }
  (*c).flags = if lapses {(*c).flags | cellLapses} else {(*c).flags & ~cellLapses};
  mem.writeRaw[Reply](&(*c).reply as *Reply, r);
  let armedWord = ((*c).word.load() & ~cellStateMask) | cellArmed;
  (*ts).armed.add(1u64);
  (*c).word.store(armedWord);
  wheelLock(ts);
  let wh = &mut (*ts).wheel;
  if wh.isEmpty() {
    // Its now brought up to date, so that "within a tick" is judged from here
    wh.expired(time.Instant.fromNanos(now), &mut (*ts).expiries);
    (*ts).expiries.clear();
  }
  (*c).entry = wh.insert(time.Instant.fromNanos(due), u64.from(c as usize));
  if due < nextOf(ts) {
    match wh.nextExpiry() {
      case let Some(t) {(*ts).next.storeOrdered(t.nanos(), MemOrder.Relaxed);}
      else {(*ts).next.storeOrdered(due, MemOrder.Relaxed);}
    }
  }
  wheelUnlock(ts);
  tally(&(*ts).arms, 1u64);
  // The Reply is the cell's from the store of the Armed word: 'f' and 'r' are
  // not used after it
  match (*c).group {
    case let Some(g) {
      g.watchHere(&CellWake(c, armedWord));
      g.watchWorkerAbove((*ts).index, &WorkerWake((*ts).index));
      // After the registrations: a cancel before them is seen here, one after
      // reaches the cell's Wakeup or the worker's
      if g.isCancelled() {
        let seen, ok = (*c).word.compareSwap(armedWord, (armedWord & ~cellStateMask) | cellTaken);
        if ok {
          cellCancelHere(ts, c);
        }
      }
    }
    else {}
  }
}

// The owner has taken an armed cell for its group's cancel: answered, freed
fn cellCancelHere(ts: *TimerStore, c: *TimerCell) {
  (*ts).armed.sub(1u64);
  (*ts).cancels.addOrdered(1u64, MemOrder.Relaxed);
  let o = cancelOutcome(&(*c).group);
  var r = cellReply(c);
  let f = (*c).answer;
  cellFree(ts, c);
  f(&mut r, o);
}

// Whether the owner's step has anything to do (workerMain asks between turns)
fn timersPending(ts: *TimerStore) bool {
  nextOf(ts) != noDue || (*ts).retire.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed) != 0usize
    || (*ts).sweep.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed) != 0u32
    || (timersStopped.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed) != 0u32 && (*ts).waiters.load() != 0u64)
}

// THE STEP, the owner's, between turns and before it parks: the retired cells
// freed; once the stop has begun, every armed cell dropped; a sweep if an
// ancestor's cancel asked; the due cells fired. True if it answered anything
fn timersStep(ts: *TimerStore) bool {
  if (*ts).retire.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed) != 0usize {
    timersDrain(ts);
  }
  if timersStopped.load() != 0u32 {
    // A sweep asked for is not made once the stop has begun, and the ask is let go (idle looks at
    // 'sweep' too, and does not leave it standing: row 531)
    (*ts).sweep.store(0u32);
    timersDropAll(ts);
    return false;
  }
  var any = false;
  if (*ts).sweep.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed) != 0u32 {
    (*ts).sweep.store(0u32);
    any = timersSweep(ts);
  }
  if nextOf(ts) != noDue {
    let now = time.Instant.now();
    if now.nanos() >= nextOf(ts) {
      any = timersFire(ts, now) || any;
    }
  }
  any
}

// The retire stack, taken whole and freed
fn timersDrain(ts: *TimerStore) {
  var c = (*ts).retire.swap(0usize) as *TimerCell;
  while c as usize != 0usize {
    let nx = (*c).retired;
    (*c).retired = null;
    cellFree(ts, c);
    c = nx;
  }
}

// The due cells: each taken by the CAS out of Armed and answered, Done or, for
// a deadline before its time, TimedOut. One a cancel took first is left to the
// retire stack
fn timersFire(ts: *TimerStore, now: time.Instant) bool {
  let wh = &mut (*ts).wheel;
  wheelLock(ts);
  wh.expired(now, &mut (*ts).expiries);
  wheelUnlock(ts);
  var any = false;
  var k = 0usize;
  while k < (*ts).expiries.len() {
    let tok = (*ts).expiries[k].token;
    let c = usize.from(tok) as *TimerCell;
    let id = (*ts).expiries[k].id;
    k = k + 1usize;
    if (tok & heldBit) != 0u64 {
      // a held cell's entry (THE HELD TIMER): its own step
      any = heldFire(ts, tok, now.nanos()) || any;
      continue;
    }
    if (*c).entry != id {
      continue;
    }
    (*c).entry = TimerId.none();
    let w = (*c).word.load();
    if (w & cellStateMask) != cellArmed {
      continue;
    }
    let seen, ok = (*c).word.compareSwap(w, (w & ~cellStateMask) | cellTaken);
    if !ok {
      continue;
    }
    (*ts).armed.sub(1u64);
    tally(&(*ts).fires, 1u64);
    let o = if ((*c).flags & cellLapses) != 0u32 {timerTimedOut} else {timerDone};
    var r = cellReply(c);
    let f = (*c).answer;
    cellRecycle(ts, c);
    f(&mut r, o);
    any = true;
  }
  (*ts).expiries.clear();
  wheelLock(ts);
  nextSet(ts);
  wheelUnlock(ts);
  any
}

// THE DEPUTY (row 485): one overdue worker's due cells fired in its stead,
// by the monitor for a worker stuck in a turn (not 'parked'), or by the poller
// for a parked one ('parked': its 'due' published, poller.cone). 'now' is the
// deputy's reading; 'sc' its scratch (the owner's is the owner's). How many it
// answered, the held cells' fires (heldFire, with the word let go and the stop
// looked at above) counted with the rest, as the poller's caller takes a count
// as work found. Not for a stopped runtime, a worker whose 'due' says the other
// case, or a wheel the owner holds this instant (the owner is running and will
// fire what is due; the deputy looks again at its next beat)
fn timersDeputy(ts: *TimerStore, now: time.Instant, sc: &mut DeputyScratch, parked: bool) u64 {
  if timersStopped.load() != 0u32 || ((*ts).due.load() != 0i64) != parked {
    return 0u64;
  }
  let nx = nextOf(ts);
  if nx == noDue || now.nanos() < nx {
    return 0u64;
  }
  if !wheelTry(ts) {
    return 0u64;
  }
  sc.expiries.clear();
  sc.won.clear();
  sc.held.clear();
  let wh = &mut (*ts).wheel;
  wh.expired(now, &mut sc.expiries);
  var k = 0usize;
  while k < sc.expiries.len() {
    let tok = sc.expiries[k].token;
    let c = usize.from(tok) as *TimerCell;
    let id = sc.expiries[k].id;
    k = k + 1usize;
    if (tok & heldBit) != 0u64 {
      // a held cell's entry (THE HELD TIMER): heldFire, once the word is let go
      // (a refile inserts in this wheel)
      sc.held.push(tok);
      continue;
    }
    if (*c).entry != id {
      continue;
    }
    // Out of the wheel now: the owner's free of it, if a cancel took it, need not look
    (*c).entry = TimerId.none();
    let w = (*c).word.load();
    if (w & cellStateMask) != cellArmed {
      continue;
    }
    let seen, ok = (*c).word.compareSwap(w, (w & ~cellStateMask) | cellTaken);
    if !ok {
      continue;
    }
    (*ts).armed.sub(1u64);
    sc.won.push(c as usize);
  }
  nextSet(ts);
  wheelUnlock(ts);
  // The lock is let go before any answer: the cells won are this thread's alone
  k = 0usize;
  while k < sc.won.len() {
    let c = sc.won[k] as *TimerCell;
    k = k + 1usize;
    (*ts).deputyFires.addOrdered(1u64, MemOrder.Relaxed);
    let o = if ((*c).flags & cellLapses) != 0u32 {timerTimedOut} else {timerDone};
    var r = cellReply(c);
    let f = (*c).answer;
    f(&mut r, o);
    cellRetire(c);
  }
  // The held entries, by the same per-entry step as the owner's (THE HELD TIMER)
  var n = u64.from(sc.won.len());
  k = 0usize;
  while k < sc.held.len() {
    let tok = sc.held[k];
    k = k + 1usize;
    if heldFire(ts, tok, now.nanos()) {
      n = n + 1u64;
    }
  }
  n
}

// The monitor's scratch for THE DEPUTY
struct DeputyScratch {
  expiries: List[Expiry];
  won: List[usize];
  held: List[u64];
}

fn deputyScratch() DeputyScratch {
  DeputyScratch(List[Expiry](), List[usize](), List[u64]())
}

// Every armed cell whose group is cancelled (an ancestor's cancel), answered
fn timersSweep(ts: *TimerStore) bool {
  var any = false;
  var ch = (*ts).chunks;
  while ch as usize != 0usize {
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < cellsPerChunk {
      let c = (*ch).cells + i;
      i = i + 1usize;
      let w = (*c).word.load();
      if (w & cellStateMask) == cellArmed && cellCancelled(c) {
        let seen, ok = (*c).word.compareSwap(w, (w & ~cellStateMask) | cellTaken);
        if ok {
          cellCancelHere(ts, c);
          any = true;
        }
      } else if (w & cellStateMask) == cellHeld && cellCancelled(c) {
        any = heldEnd(c, w, lifeOf((*c).hword.load()), true) || any;
      }
    }
    ch = (*ch).next;
  }
  any
}

// The stop's drop: every armed cell taken and its Reply let go unanswered
fn timersDropAll(ts: *TimerStore) {
  if (*ts).armed.load() == 0u64 && (*ts).waiters.load() == 0u64 {
    return;
  }
  var ch = (*ts).chunks;
  while ch as usize != 0usize {
    var i = 0usize;
    while i < cellsPerChunk {
      let c = (*ch).cells + i;
      i = i + 1usize;
      let w = (*c).word.load();
      if (w & cellStateMask) == cellArmed {
        let seen, ok = (*c).word.compareSwap(w, (w & ~cellStateMask) | cellTaken);
        if ok {
          (*ts).armed.sub(1u64);
          (*ts).dropped.addOrdered(1u64, MemOrder.Relaxed);
          let r = cellReply(c);
          cellFree(ts, c);
        }
      } else if (w & cellStateMask) == cellHeld {
        heldDrop(c);
      }
    }
    ch = (*ch).next;
  }
  wheelLock(ts);
  (*ts).next.storeOrdered(noDue, MemOrder.Relaxed);
  wheelUnlock(ts);
}

// THE STOP's part (stopWorkers, first): no cell fires or is answered from now
// on, and every worker with armed cells drops them, woken for it; this returns
// once none is armed. The workers still run
fn timersStop(s: *Sched) {
  timersStopped.store(1u32);
  var i = 0u32;
  while i < (*s).nworkers {
    let ts = timerStoreOf(i);
    if ts as usize != 0usize {
      while (*ts).armed.load() != 0u64 || (*ts).waiters.load() != 0u64 {
        wakeNamed(s, workerAt(s, i));
        thread.sleep(time.Duration.fromMicros(50i64));
      }
    }
    i = i + 1u32;
  }
}

// The earliest instant this worker must wake at, for its park; noDue if none
fn timersNext() i64 {
  if myTimers == 0usize {
    return noDue;
  }
  nextOf(myTimers as *TimerStore)
}

// THE MONITOR's part: the earliest 'next' of a worker that is not parked but
// has cells armed (the deputy's concern; noDue if no such worker), for the
// monitor to pace itself by, no faster than its base tick. A parked worker's
// cells are the poller's (poller.cone, KEEPING TIME)
fn timersRunningNext(s: *Sched) i64 {
  var running = noDue;
  var i = 0u32;
  while i < (*s).nworkers {
    let ts = timerStoreOf(i);
    if ts as usize != 0usize && (*ts).due.load() == 0i64 {
      let nx = nextOf(ts);
      if nx < running {
        running = nx;
      }
    }
    i = i + 1u32;
  }
  running
}

// A TEST HOOK, not part of the API (aio's worker-timer tests): the workers'
// timer counts summed: cells armed now, arms, fires, cancels (and sweeps)
// answered, and cells dropped at the stop; and of the held timers (THE HELD
// TIMER, the spec's counters), the cells held now, their entries in the wheels
// now (live and dead), the earlier moves in place and across workers, the
// refiles and the dead entries discarded
pub struct TimerStats {
  pub armed: u64;
  pub arms: u64;
  pub fires: u64;
  pub cancels: u64;
  pub dropped: u64;
  pub held: u64;
  pub heldEntries: u64;
  pub movesInPlace: u64;
  pub movesAcross: u64;
  pub refiles: u64;
  pub deadEntries: u64;
}

pub fn timerStats() TimerStats {
  var st = TimerStats(0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64, 0u64);
  var ins = 0u64;
  var outs = 0u64;
  let n = timerTableLen.load();
  var i = 0u32;
  while i < n {
    let ts = timerStoreOf(i);
    if ts as usize != 0usize {
      st.armed = st.armed + (*ts).armed.load();
      st.arms = st.arms + (*ts).arms.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
      st.fires = st.fires + (*ts).fires.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed) + (*ts).deputyFires.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
      st.cancels = st.cancels + (*ts).cancels.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
      st.dropped = st.dropped + (*ts).dropped.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
      st.held = st.held + (*ts).held.load();
      ins = ins + (*ts).heldIn.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
      outs = outs + (*ts).heldOut.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
      st.movesInPlace = st.movesInPlace + (*ts).movesInPlace.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
      st.movesAcross = st.movesAcross + (*ts).movesAcross.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
      st.refiles = st.refiles + (*ts).refiles.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
      st.deadEntries = st.deadEntries + (*ts).deadEntries.loadOrdered(MemOrder.Relaxed);
    }
    i = i + 1u32;
  }
  st.heldEntries = if ins >= outs {ins - outs} else {0u64};
  st
}

// THE HELD TIMER (row 500; "aio and http"'s re-armable timer spec, 18 Nov
// 2026). Timer is a Move value in an actor's state holding one deadline or
// none, and, from its first set or next() on a worker, one HELD CELL of the
// stores above for its whole life. The cell is the timer's home and belongs to
// no worker but its store's (which frees it); only its live WHEEL ENTRY belongs
// to a worker, the FILER, and that may be any worker's wheel. The program
// loops on 'while await timer.next() { ... }' and sets the deadline after
// each turn:
//   - a LATER move is one store to 'want': the old entry comes up early at its
//     filer, which sees the later 'want' and files it again (a refile), with no
//     turn of the actor;
//   - an EARLIER move on the filer cancels the entry and inserts it again in
//     place (the wheel's free list reuses the entry just freed); on another
//     worker it takes the word (one compare-and-swap) and files a new entry in
//     its own wheel, the old one left DEAD for its wheel to discard when it
//     comes up (it names an old move generation, or an old filer);
//   - THE FIRE, at the filer's step (heldFire, the one per-entry step, which
//     the deputy, timersDeputy, also calls for a stuck filer): due with a
//     next() parked, the word goes from hWaiter to hInflight and an ARRIVE
//     SLOT is published to the actor, the waiter's count with it; timerArrive
//     then runs on the actor's own thread and decides again from 'want' there:
//     due, the program resumes with true and the deadline is cleared; moved
//     later or cleared since the filer looked, the waiter is put back and
//     nothing runs. A next() that finds its deadline already passed publishes
//     the same slot to itself, never an answer of true, since a set or clear
//     queued to the actor before it runs first (tests/heldqueued.cone). So no
//     resume is stale and none is doubled: only the winner
//     of a CAS that clears hWaiter publishes, or answers;
//   - the end: stop(), the group's cancel (Timer.within), or the Timer
//     dropped, sets hEnded; a parked next() answers false (an arrive in flight
//     answers false at its arrival), and so does every later one.
// The word, 'hword': flags (below) in the low 16 bits, the filer's index in
// bits 16-31, the MOVE GENERATION in 32-47 (each entry's token carries it, with
// the cell's address and heldBit) and the LIFE in 48-63 (moved at each take;
// the cell's Wakeup names it). 'hentry' is the filer's entry, written only by
// whoever holds hBusy: a worker takes hBusy, with the filer's place, by the CAS
// that makes it the filer or refiles there, and drops it once 'hentry' is
// written; an earlier move that finds another worker's hBusy sets hMoved
// instead, and that filer looks at 'want' again before it lets go. 'want' is
// written by the holder alone, on the actor's thread; every hand-off of an
// actor orders those stores before timerArrive's read.
// A parked next() holds a count of its actor, as every await does, so an
// actor with its loop parked lives until stop() or the cancel; one dropped with
// no waiter frees the cell at its end (or, its arrive still in flight, leaves
// that to timerArrive). Dead entries and a stale Wakeup find the cell's
// generation or life moved, and cells are never unmapped. At THE STOP each
// store's walk lets its parked waiters go unanswered, as it does armed sleeps.
// Every wheel operation here runs on the wheel's owner, under THE WHEEL WORD,
// except THE DEPUTY's (row 485): for a worker stuck in one turn the monitor
// takes the due entries out and calls heldFire for the held ones, with the word
// let go, so a refile there inserts in the stuck worker's wheel from the
// monitor's thread. So every change the owner makes to a filed entry in its own
// wheel first takes the entry by a CAS of 'hword' (hBusy, or clearing hFiled),
// as a fire does, and the counts both add to are atomic adds.
const hFiled = 1u64;       // an entry of the current move generation is in the filer's wheel
const hWaiter = 2u64;      // a next() is parked: the cell holds its Reply
const hInflight = 4u64;    // an arrive slot is on its way to the actor: the cell holds the Reply still
const hEnded = 8u64;       // stopped, cancelled or dropped: next() answers false
const hByGroup = 16u64;    // ... and it was the group's cancel
const hBusy = 32u64;       // the filer is writing 'hentry'
const hMoved = 64u64;      // an earlier move came while it was: the filer looks again
const hGone = 128u64;      // the Timer was dropped with an arrive in flight: timerArrive frees the cell
const hFilerMask = 0xFFFF0000u64;
const hGenMask = 0xFFFF00000000u64;
const hLifeMask = 0xFFFF000000000000u64;
const heldBit = 1u64;                      // a held cell's token (a cell's address has its low three bits clear)
const heldAddrMask = 0x0000FFFFFFFFFFF8u64;

fn filerOf(w: u64) u64 {(w & hFilerMask) >> 16u64}
fn genOf(w: u64) u64 {(w & hGenMask) >> 32u64}
fn lifeOf(w: u64) u64 {(w & hLifeMask) >> 48u64}
fn withFiler(w: u64, i: u32) u64 {(w & ~hFilerMask) | (u64.from(i) << 16u64)}

fn genBumped(w: u64) u64 {
  let g = genOf(w);
  let n = if g == 0xFFFFu64 {0u64} else {g + 1u64};
  (w & ~hGenMask) | (n << 32u64)
}

fn lifeBumped(w: u64) u64 {
  let g = lifeOf(w);
  let n = if g == 0xFFFFu64 {0u64} else {g + 1u64};
  (w & ~hLifeMask) | (n << 48u64)
}

// A wheel entry's id as one word, and back
fn idWord(id: TimerId) u64 {
  if mem.sizeof[TimerId]() != 8usize {
    die("actors: a TimerId is not one word");
  }
  var x = id;
  mem.readRaw[u64](&mut x as *u64)
}

fn idOfWord(w: u64) TimerId {
  var x = w;
  mem.readRaw[TimerId](&mut x as *TimerId)
}

// This worker's index for comparing with a filer, or none
fn hereIndex(ts: *TimerStore) u64 {
  if ts as usize == 0usize {0xFFFFFFFFu64} else {u64.from((*ts).index)}
}

// A cell for a Timer, from this worker's store: its new life begun, its
// group's Wakeup registered once for that life
fn heldTake(xs: *TimerStore, g: &Option[CancelGroup], want: i64) *TimerCell {
  let c = cellTake(xs);
  let sw = ((*c).word.load() & ~cellStateMask) | cellHeld;
  (*c).word.store(sw);
  let hw = lifeBumped((*c).hword.load() & (hGenMask | hLifeMask));
  (*c).hword.store(hw);
  (*c).want.store(want);
  (*c).hentry.store(0u64);
  mem.writeRaw[Option[CancelGroup]](&(*c).group as *Option[CancelGroup], *g);
  (*xs).held.add(1u64);
  match (*c).group {
    case let Some(gr) {
      gr.watchHere(&HeldWake(c, sw, lifeOf(hw)));
      gr.watchWorkerAbove((*xs).index, &WorkerWake((*xs).index));
      // after the registrations, as timerStart's: a cancel before them is seen here
      if gr.isCancelled() {
        heldEnd(c, sw, lifeOf(hw), true);
      }
    }
    else {}
  }
  c
}

// The cell freed at the end of its life: by its store's owner, or retired to it
fn heldRelease(c: *TimerCell) {
  let b = (*c).store;
  (*b).held.sub(1u64);
  if myTimers == b as usize {
    cellFree(b, c);
  } else {
    cellRetire(c);
  }
}

// An entry for the cell in this wheel, its token naming the move generation
// 'gen'. 'fresh': not inside the fire step, so an empty wheel's now may be
// brought up to date first (as timerStart does; the owner's alone, since it
// uses the owner's scratch). Under THE WHEEL WORD: the deputy refiles here too
fn heldInsert(ts: *TimerStore, c: *TimerCell, at: i64, gen: u64, fresh: bool) u64 {
  wheelLock(ts);
  let wh = &mut (*ts).wheel;
  if fresh && wh.isEmpty() {
    wh.expired(time.Instant.now(), &mut (*ts).expiries);
    (*ts).expiries.clear();
  }
  let id = wh.insert(time.Instant.fromNanos(at), u64.from(c as usize) | (gen << 48u64) | heldBit);
  if at < nextOf(ts) {
    match wh.nextExpiry() {
      case let Some(t) {(*ts).next.storeOrdered(t.nanos(), MemOrder.Relaxed);}
      else {(*ts).next.storeOrdered(at, MemOrder.Relaxed);}
    }
  }
  wheelUnlock(ts);
  heldCount(&(*ts).heldIn);
  idWord(id)
}

// A held entry cancelled in this wheel (under THE WHEEL WORD)
fn heldCancelIn(ts: *TimerStore, idw: u64) {
  wheelLock(ts);
  let wh = &mut (*ts).wheel;
  let out = wh.cancel(idOfWord(idw));
  wheelUnlock(ts);
  if out {
    heldCount(&(*ts).heldOut);
  }
}

// One more on a held count that the owner and the deputy both add to (an
// atomic add, so neither's is lost; tally is the owner's alone)
fn heldCount(n: &Atomic[u64]) {
  n.addOrdered(1u64, MemOrder.Relaxed);
}

// The filer's part once it holds hBusy (its CAS made it the filer, or refiled
// there): the entry inserted at 'at' and written, then hBusy dropped; an
// earlier move that came meanwhile (hMoved) is looked at first
fn heldInstall(ts: *TimerStore, c: *TimerCell, at0: i64, fresh: bool) {
  var at = at0;
  let gen = genOf((*c).hword.load());
  var id = heldInsert(ts, c, at, gen, fresh);
  (*c).hentry.store(id);
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & hMoved) != 0u64 {
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, w & ~hMoved);
      if ok {
        let nw = (*c).want.load();
        if nw < at {
          heldCancelIn(ts, id);
          at = nw;
          id = heldInsert(ts, c, at, gen, fresh);
          (*c).hentry.store(id);
        }
      }
      continue;
    }
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, w & ~hBusy);
    if ok {
      return;
    }
  }
}

// The deadline filed on this worker, if one is set and nothing is filed or in
// flight (the holder, on the actor's thread)
fn heldFileHere(xs: *TimerStore, c: *TimerCell) {
  if xs as usize == 0usize {
    return;
  }
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & (hEnded | hInflight | hFiled)) != 0u64 || (*c).want.load() == noDue {
      return;
    }
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, withFiler(genBumped(w), (*xs).index) | hFiled | hBusy);
    if ok {
      heldInstall(xs, c, (*c).want.load(), true);
      return;
    }
  }
}

// set(at), the holder's
fn heldSet(xs: *TimerStore, c: *TimerCell, at: i64) {
  let old = (*c).want.load();
  (*c).want.store(at);
  if xs as usize == 0usize {
    return;
  }
  let mine = u64.from((*xs).index);
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & (hEnded | hInflight)) != 0u64 {
      // ended; or a delivery is in flight, and timerArrive decides from 'want'
      return;
    }
    if (w & hFiled) == 0u64 {
      heldFileHere(xs, c);
      return;
    }
    if at >= old {
      // later: the filer refiles when the old entry comes up
      return;
    }
    if (w & hBusy) != 0u64 {
      // the filer is filing it now (another worker, or the deputy refiling in
      // this wheel): it looks at 'want' again before it lets go
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, w | hMoved);
      if ok {
        if filerOf(w) == mine {
          tally(&(*xs).movesInPlace, 1u64);
        } else {
          tally(&(*xs).movesAcross, 1u64);
        }
        return;
      }
      continue;
    }
    if filerOf(w) == mine {
      // earlier, in place: cancel and insert in this wheel. The entry is taken
      // first (hBusy, and a new move generation), since the deputy may fire this
      // wheel's entries meanwhile: one it has out already is then dead
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, genBumped(w) | hBusy);
      if ok {
        heldCancelIn(xs, (*c).hentry.load());
        tally(&(*xs).movesInPlace, 1u64);
        heldInstall(xs, c, at, true);
        return;
      }
      continue;
    }
    // earlier, on another worker: this one becomes the filer; the old entry is dead
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, withFiler(genBumped(w), (*xs).index) | hBusy);
    if ok {
      tally(&(*xs).movesAcross, 1u64);
      heldInstall(xs, c, at, true);
      return;
    }
  }
}

// clear(), the holder's: no deadline; an entry in this wheel is cancelled in
// place, one elsewhere is left to come up and find none
fn heldClear(xs: *TimerStore, c: *TimerCell) {
  (*c).want.store(noDue);
  let mine = hereIndex(xs);
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & hFiled) == 0u64 || (w & hBusy) != 0u64 || filerOf(w) != mine {
      return;
    }
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, w & ~hFiled);
    if ok {
      heldCancelIn(xs, (*c).hentry.load());
      return;
    }
  }
}

// stop(), the holder's: ended; a parked next() answered false (to this very
// actor, which is running, so nothing is woken)
fn heldStop(xs: *TimerStore, c: *TimerCell) {
  (*c).want.store(noDue);
  let mine = hereIndex(xs);
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & hEnded) != 0u64 {
      return;
    }
    var nw = w | hEnded;
    let take = (w & hWaiter) != 0u64 && (w & hInflight) == 0u64;
    if take {nw = nw & ~hWaiter;}
    let here = (w & hFiled) != 0u64 && (w & hBusy) == 0u64 && filerOf(w) == mine;
    if here {nw = nw & ~hFiled;}
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, nw);
    if ok {
      if here {
        heldCancelIn(xs, (*c).hentry.load());
      }
      if take {
        (*(*c).store).waiters.sub(1u64);
        var r = cellReply(c);
        answerNowIn[bool](&mut r, false);
      }
      return;
    }
  }
}

// The end by the group's cancel (its Wakeup, any thread, or the sweep for an
// ancestor's), for the cell's life 'life' while its word is still 'sw': a
// parked next() is answered false here, as a cell's cancel answers on the
// cancelling thread
fn heldEnd(c: *TimerCell, sw: u64, life: u64, byGroup: bool) bool {
  while true {
    if (*c).word.load() != sw {
      return false;
    }
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if lifeOf(w) != life || (w & hEnded) != 0u64 {
      return false;
    }
    var nw = w | hEnded;
    if byGroup {nw = nw | hByGroup;}
    let take = (w & hWaiter) != 0u64 && (w & hInflight) == 0u64;
    if take {nw = nw & ~hWaiter;}
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, nw);
    if ok {
      if take {
        (*(*c).store).waiters.sub(1u64);
        (*(*c).store).cancels.addOrdered(1u64, MemOrder.Relaxed);
        var r = cellReply(c);
        answerNowIn[bool](&mut r, false);
      }
      return true;
    }
  }
  false
}

// A held cell's Wakeup in its group's registry (watchHere), for one life of
// the cell. Sendable on trust, as CellWake is: the cell is never freed
struct HeldWake is Sendable {
  cell: *TimerCell;
  word: u64;
  life: u64;

  pub fn signal(self: &) bool {
    if timersStopped.load() != 0u32 {
      return false;
    }
    heldEnd(cell, word, life, true)
  }

  pub fn isGone(self: &) bool {(*cell).word.load() != word}
}

// THE STOP's walk, for a held cell of this store: a parked next() let go
// unanswered (its count, its group note and its operation, as Reply.final does)
fn heldDrop(c: *TimerCell) {
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & hWaiter) == 0u64 {
      return;
    }
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, (w & ~hWaiter) | hEnded);
    if ok {
      (*(*c).store).waiters.sub(1u64);
      (*(*c).store).dropped.addOrdered(1u64, MemOrder.Relaxed);
      let r = cellReply(c);
      return;
    }
  }
}

// THE FIRE for one held entry that came up in this wheel (the owner's step, and
// THE DEPUTY's for a stuck owner, each with the wheel's word let go). Dead (an
// old filer, move generation or life): discarded. Ended or no deadline: nothing
// filed. Moved later: filed again here. Due with a waiter: the arrive slot
// published. Due with none: nothing filed, and the next next() answers at once.
// True if it published
fn heldFire(ts: *TimerStore, tok: u64, now: i64) bool {
  heldCount(&(*ts).heldOut);
  let c = usize.from(tok & heldAddrMask) as *TimerCell;
  let tg = tok >> 48u64;
  let mine = u64.from((*ts).index);
  if ((*c).word.load() & cellStateMask) != cellHeld {
    heldCount(&(*ts).deadEntries);
    return false;
  }
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & hFiled) == 0u64 || (w & hBusy) != 0u64 || filerOf(w) != mine || genOf(w) != tg {
      heldCount(&(*ts).deadEntries);
      return false;
    }
    let want = (*c).want.load();
    if (w & hEnded) != 0u64 || want == noDue {
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, w & ~hFiled);
      if ok {
        return false;
      }
    } else if want > now {
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, genBumped(w) | hBusy);
      if ok {
        heldCount(&(*ts).refiles);
        heldInstall(ts, c, want, false);
        return false;
      }
    } else if (w & hWaiter) != 0u64 {
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, (w & ~(hFiled | hWaiter)) | hInflight);
      if ok {
        (*(*c).store).waiters.sub(1u64);
        heldPublish(c);
        return true;
      }
    } else {
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, w & ~hFiled);
      if ok {
        return false;
      }
    }
  }
  false
}

// The arrive slot, published to the waiting actor as pushFuture publishes a
// future's: its resume function timerArrive, its id the cell. The count the
// waiter's Reply held goes with it (the scheduler's owner, or let go)
fn heldPublish(c: *TimerCell) {
  let h = (*c).reply.to;
  // THE STOP'S GATE, for a plain thread (a deputy): refused, the waiter is let go unanswered
  let plain = me == 0usize && stopperHere == 0usize;
  if plain && !gateEnter() {
    refuseSend(0u64);
    let r = cellReply(c);
    return;
  }
  if running.load() == 0usize {
    die("actors: a timer's fire after the runtime stopped");
  }
  let cl = claim(h);
  var cause = 0u64;
  if traceLayerOn(traceLayerActors) {
    cause = traceSend(h, traceKindReply);
  }
  mem.atomicStore[u64](ccause(cl.slot), cause, MemOrder.Relaxed);
  let p = payloadOf(cl.slot);
  var rf = &timerArrive;
  *(p as **u8) = mem.readRaw[*u8](&mut rf as *(*u8));
  *((p + 8usize) as *u64) = u64.from(c as usize);
  *((p + replyHead) as **u8) = null;
  let waited = publish(cl, kindReply + 1u64);
  if wakeAfter(h, cl, waited) {
    schedule(h);
  } else {
    let release = (*h).release;
    release(h);
  }
  if plain {
    gateLeave();
  }
}

// The arrive slot reached the actor (its resume function; 'id' is the cell).
// The decision is made again here, on the holder's thread: ended, false; due,
// the deadline cleared and true; otherwise the waiter put back (a count of the
// actor taken for it again), the deadline filed here if one is set, and the
// program sees nothing
fn timerArrive(st: *u8, id: u64, data: *u8) {
  let c = usize.from(id) as *TimerCell;
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & hEnded) != 0u64 {
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, w & ~hInflight);
      if ok {
        heldResume(st, c, false);
        if (w & hGone) != 0u64 {
          heldRelease(c);
        }
        return;
      }
      continue;
    }
    let want = (*c).want.load();
    if want != noDue && want <= time.Instant.now().nanos() {
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, w & ~hInflight);
      if ok {
        (*c).want.store(noDue);
        heldResume(st, c, true);
        return;
      }
      continue;
    }
    let h = (*c).reply.to;
    holdHeader(h);
    (*(*c).store).waiters.add(1u64);
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, (w & ~hInflight) | hWaiter);
    if ok {
      heldFileHere(timersHere(), c);
      return;
    }
    (*(*c).store).waiters.sub(1u64);
    let release = (*h).release;
    release(h);
  }
}

// What the program's resume needs of the waiter's Reply, which is spent here:
// its count went with the arrive slot, and its operation is counted spent
struct HeldRun {
  run: *u8;
  id: u64;
  hasId: bool;
}

fn heldSpend(c: *TimerCell) HeldRun {
  var r = cellReply(c);
  let hr = HeldRun(r.at, r.id, (r.meta & replyHasId) != 0u64);
  spend(&mut r);
  hr
}

// The program resumed with v, as a reply's slot resumes it (resumeSlot): the
// seam's resume function called directly, the value on this stack, in the
// group noted at its await
fn heldResume(st: *u8, c: *TimerCell, v: bool) {
  let hr = heldSpend(c);
  var val = v;
  let data = &mut val as *bool as *u8;
  if (hr.id & groupBit) == 0u64 {
    heldCall(hr.run, st, hr.hasId, hr.id, data);
    return;
  }
  let node = usize.from(hr.id ^ groupBit) as *GNode;
  groupTake(node);
  let w = (*node).w;
  let g = mem.readRaw[CancelGroup](&(*node).g as *CancelGroup);
  libc.free(node as *u8);
  curGroup = &g as *CancelGroup as usize;
  heldCall(hr.run, st, hr.hasId, w, data);
  curGroup = 0usize;
}

fn heldCall(run: *u8, st: *u8, hasId: bool, id: u64, data: *u8) {
  var f = run;
  if hasId {
    let fp = mem.readRaw[&fn(s: *u8, id: u64, data: *u8)](&mut f as *(&fn(s: *u8, id: u64, data: *u8)));
    fp(st, id, data);
  } else {
    let fp = mem.readRaw[&fn(s: *u8, data: *u8)](&mut f as *(&fn(s: *u8, data: *u8)));
    fp(st, data);
  }
}

// next()'s start, at the seam (on the actor's worker): ended, false at once;
// due, an arrive slot published to the actor at once, as the fire publishes
// one, so that timerArrive decides again when it is reached (a set or clear
// already queued to the actor runs before it, and a resume of true then would
// be stale); otherwise the Reply kept and the waiter set, and the deadline
// filed here if it is set and nothing is filed
fn heldStart(ctx: *u8, rp: Reply) {
  let c = ctx as *TimerCell;
  var r = rp;
  let xs = timersHere();
  if xs as usize == 0usize || timersStopped.load() != 0u32 {
    // the stop has begun: let go unanswered, as a sleep is
    return;
  }
  let w0 = (*c).hword.load();
  if (w0 & (hWaiter | hInflight)) != 0u64 {
    die("actors: a Timer's next() awaited while another is");
  }
  if (w0 & hEnded) != 0u64 {
    answerNowIn[bool](&mut r, false);
    return;
  }
  let want = (*c).want.load();
  if want != noDue && want <= time.Instant.now().nanos() {
    // nothing stays filed while the slot is in flight, as at the fire: an
    // entry here is cancelled, one elsewhere left dead (hFiled cleared, a new
    // move generation), once any filer writing it (hBusy) is done
    mem.writeRaw[Reply](&(*c).reply as *Reply, r);
    let mine = hereIndex(xs);
    while true {
      let w = (*c).hword.load();
      if (w & hBusy) != 0u64 {
        yieldProcessor();
        continue;
      }
      let here = (w & hFiled) != 0u64 && filerOf(w) == mine;
      let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, (genBumped(w) & ~hFiled) | hInflight);
      if ok {
        if here {
          heldCancelIn(xs, (*c).hentry.load());
        }
        break;
      }
    }
    heldPublish(c);
    return;
  }
  mem.writeRaw[Reply](&(*c).reply as *Reply, r);
  (*(*c).store).waiters.add(1u64);
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & hEnded) != 0u64 {
      (*(*c).store).waiters.sub(1u64);
      var back = cellReply(c);
      answerNowIn[bool](&mut back, false);
      return;
    }
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, w | hWaiter);
    if ok {
      break;
    }
  }
  heldFileHere(xs, c);
}

// next()'s Awaitable dying unawaited: the cell is the Timer's, so nothing
fn heldNoDrop(ctx: *u8) {}

// The Timer gone (its final): ended, its entry here cancelled, a parked next()
// answered false (the Timer was replaced or dropped by its own actor while its
// loop waited), and the cell freed, or, with an arrive in flight, left for
// timerArrive to free
fn heldFinal(c: *TimerCell) {
  let ts = myTimers as *TimerStore;
  let mine = hereIndex(ts);
  var here = false;
  var take = false;
  var flying = false;
  while true {
    let w = (*c).hword.load();
    if (w & hBusy) != 0u64 {
      // another worker, or the deputy refiling in this wheel, is writing the
      // entry: a few instructions (the cell must not be freed under it)
      yieldProcessor();
      continue;
    }
    take = (w & hWaiter) != 0u64 && (w & hInflight) == 0u64;
    here = (w & hFiled) != 0u64 && filerOf(w) == mine;
    flying = (w & hInflight) != 0u64;
    var nw = genBumped(w | hEnded) & ~hWaiter;
    if here {nw = nw & ~hFiled;}
    if flying {nw = nw | hGone;}
    let seen, ok = (*c).hword.compareSwap(w, nw);
    if ok {
      break;
    }
  }
  if here {
    heldCancelIn(ts, (*c).hentry.load());
  }
  if take {
    (*(*c).store).waiters.sub(1u64);
    var r = cellReply(c);
    answerNowIn[bool](&mut r, false);
  }
  if !flying {
    heldRelease(c);
  }
}

// A re-armable timer, held in an actor's state for the actor's life (THE HELD
// TIMER, above): one deadline or none, and a loop on 'while await
// timer.next() { ... }' that resumes once each time the deadline comes. Move,
// since a copy would give the cell two holders; not Sendable, since its
// deadline is written by its actor alone. Its methods are the actor's: call
// them from its behaviours (set and clear may also be called before the first
// behaviour, off the workers; the cell is then taken at the first on a worker)
pub struct Timer is Move {
  cell: *TimerCell = null;
  group: Option[CancelGroup] = None;
  pend: i64 = noDue;          // the deadline while there is no cell
  stopped: bool = false;

  // No deadline; nothing is taken until the first set or next() on a worker
  pub fn make() Timer {
    Timer()
  }

  // The same, ended by g's cancel (or its deadline's): a parked next() then
  // answers false, and cause() says why
  pub fn within(g: &CancelGroup) Timer {
    Timer(group: Some[CancelGroup](*g))
  }

  // The one deadline, replacing any: later, a store; earlier, a move of its
  // wheel entry. One already past fires at this worker's next step
  pub fn set(self: &mut, at: time.Instant) {
    let xs = timersHere();
    if self.cell as usize == 0usize {
      self.pend = at.nanos();
      if xs as usize == 0usize || self.stopped {
        return;
      }
      self.cell = heldTake(xs, &self.group, self.pend);
      heldFileHere(xs, self.cell);
      return;
    }
    heldSet(xs, self.cell, at.nanos());
  }

  // No deadline. A parked next() stays parked
  pub fn clear(self: &mut) {
    self.pend = noDue;
    if self.cell as usize == 0usize {
      return;
    }
    heldClear(timersHere(), self.cell);
  }

  // Ended: a parked next() answers false, and so does every later one
  pub fn stop(self: &mut) {
    self.stopped = true;
    self.pend = noDue;
    if self.cell as usize == 0usize {
      return;
    }
    heldStop(timersHere(), self.cell);
  }

  // The deadline set, if any
  pub fn deadline(self: &) Option[time.Instant] {
    let d = if self.cell as usize == 0usize {self.pend} else {(*self.cell).want.load()};
    if d == noDue {None} else {Some[time.Instant](time.Instant.fromNanos(d))}
  }

  // Wait for the deadline: true when it has come (and it is cleared), false
  // once the timer has ended. One next() may be parked at a time
  pub fn next(self: &mut) Awaitable[bool] {
    if self.cell as usize == 0usize {
      let xs = timersHere();
      if xs as usize == 0usize {
        die("actors: a Timer's next() off the workers");
      }
      self.cell = heldTake(xs, &self.group, self.pend);
      if self.stopped {
        heldStop(xs, self.cell);
      }
    }
    Awaitable[bool].of(self.cell as *u8, &heldStart, &heldNoDrop)
  }

  // Why it ended by its group (Cancelled or TimedOut); None if it has not, or
  // was stopped first
  pub fn cause(self: &) Option[Cause] {
    if self.cell as usize == 0usize || ((*self.cell).hword.load() & hByGroup) == 0u64 {
      return None;
    }
    match self.group {
      case let Some(g) {g.cause()}
      else {None}
    }
  }

  fn final(self: &uni) {
    if cell as usize != 0usize {
      heldFinal(cell);
    }
  }
}

// A TEST HOOK, not part of the API (tests/sweepatstop.cone): ask worker i for a sweep as WorkerWake.signal does,
// without waking it, so that a test can leave the ask standing where a race would (row 531). Nothing if worker i
// has made no store
pub fn askSweep(i: u32) {
  let ts = timerStoreOf(i);
  if ts as usize != 0usize {
    (*ts).sweep.store(1u32);
  }
}
